1. **An electroluminescence display device comprising:**

a substrate having a plurality of recessed portions;

a plurality of active elements disposed on the substrate and respectively associated with the recessed portions;

a reflective layer disposed at least partially within each recessed portion, the reflective layer including a contact portion electrically connected to a corresponding one of the active elements;

a transparent filling layer disposed within each recessed portion over the reflective layer;

a transparent electrode layer disposed over the transparent filling layer and electrically connected to the corresponding active element through the contact portion of the reflective layer;

an organic light-emitting layer disposed over the transparent electrode layer; and

a counter electrode disposed over the organic light-emitting layer,

wherein the reflective layer is configured both to reflect light generated by the organic light-emitting layer toward a display surface of the electroluminescence display device and to provide the contact portion for electrically coupling the transparent electrode layer to the corresponding active element.

1. An organic light-emitting diode (OLED) display apparatus comprising:

a substrate having a plurality of unit regions, each unit region including a plurality of recesses;

a plurality of active elements disposed in each unit region;

a plurality of organic light-emitting elements disposed in each unit region and electrically controlled by respective active elements of the plurality of active elements; and

at least one electrically conductive reflector disposed within a respective recess of the plurality of recesses, the electrically conductive reflector being configured to reflect light emitted by a corresponding organic light-emitting element and to provide an electrical contact for the corresponding organic light-emitting element.

A display device comprising:

a substrate including a plurality of cavities;

a transparent filler disposed within the plurality of cavities;

a plurality of transparent electrodes and an organic emissive layer disposed in association with the plurality of cavities; and

a reflective conductive material lining at least a portion of the plurality of cavities, the reflective conductive material electrically coupling at least one emissive element defined by the organic emissive layer to a corresponding driving transistor.
